{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Elohim dealt well.</b> Rashi explains what the goodness was: ״ויעש להם בתים״. But this does not seem correct, for there is a verse intervening. Therefore it appears preferable to say that it refers to that very same verse, and the meaning is: And Elohim dealt well with the midwives through the fact that the people multiplied and grew very strong — for since the midwives said to Pharaoh, ״כי חיות הנה״, they do not need us, Pharaoh said they are liars. But when he saw that the people multiplied and grew very strong, he went back and said: thus the midwives spoke truth, for it is clear to me that one or two midwives cannot suffice for a people as numerous as this."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:25.202545604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}